   "description": "Khung môn học theo syllabus FLM chính thức.",
   "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">ERW413 · Section 0 · Lesson 0.3</span>\n<h2>The 9 course learning outcomes (CLO), verbatim</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Exam questions are written against these outcomes — use them as your checklist.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM · Syllabus ID 13894 · Decision 1402/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 12/12/2025 · collected 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">ERW413 · Mục 0 · Bài 0.3</span>\n<h2>9 chuẩn đầu ra môn học (CLO), nguyên văn</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Đề thi được ra theo các chuẩn đầu ra này — dùng chúng làm danh sách tự kiểm.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: FLM · Syllabus ID 13894 · QĐ 1402/QĐ-ĐHFPT ngày 12/12/2025 · thu ngày 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>CLO</th><th>Details (verbatim)<br><small>Nội dung (nguyên văn)</small></th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>1</td><td><strong>LO1</strong></td><td>Develop emotional intelligence and critical thinking; characterize and integrate the awareness of emotional intelligence and critical thinking into writing practice<br>LO1.1 develop emotional intelligence and apply it to writing<br>LO1.2 think critically and understand how critical thinking affects reading and writing skills<br>LO1.3 identify features that boost successful writing.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>2</td><td><strong>CLO2</strong></td><td>Annotate texts and develop vocabulary<br>LO2.1 use reading to improve writing<br>LO2.2 develop annotation skills<br>LO2.3 develop vocabulary.&quot;</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>3</td><td><strong>CLO3</strong></td><td>Preview texts and work with assigned writing topics<br>LO3.1 use pre-reading strategies effectively<br>LO3.2 work with assigned writing topics<br>LO3.3 develop and narrow a topic for an essay<br>LO3.4 use pre-writing stategies to generate ideas.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>4</td><td><strong>CLO4</strong></td><td>Identify main ideas and compose effective thesis statements<br>LO4.1 identify topic sentences and implied main ideas in paragraphs<br>LO4.2 identify (implied) main ideas in essays<br>LO4.3 compose effective thesis statements.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>5</td><td><strong>CLO5</strong></td><td>Identify and use supporting details for main ideas<br>LO5.1 recognize major supporting points and supporting details in texts<br>LO5.2 use outlining or graphic organizers to identify major supporting points and supporting details<br>LO5.3 use specific supporting details in writing.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>6</td><td><strong>CLO6</strong></td><td>Identify and analyze text purposes and text patterns<br>LO6.1 identify the purpose of a text<br>LO6.2 connect purposes and text patterns<br>LO6.3 recognize, analyze and use narration/ definition/ illustration/ classification/ comparison-contrast/ cause-effect/ process analysis/ argument/ and mixed patterns in reading and writing.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>7</td><td><strong>CLO7</strong></td><td>Organize, draft and summarize texts for writing<br>LO7.1 Identify common strategies for ordering information<br>LO7.2 use information-ordering strategies in writing<br>LO7.3 use outlines and graphic organizers to analyze a text's organization<br>LO7.4 use outline to draft essays and to write detailed/brief summaries<br>LO7.5 write paraphrases.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>8</td><td><strong>CLO8</strong></td><td>write titles, introductions and conclusions effectively<br>LO8.1 analyze and create title<br>LO8.2 read, analyze and create introductions<br>LO8.3 read, analyze and create conclusions.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>9</td><td><strong>CLO9</strong></td><td>Identify, analyze and use inferrences as well as tones<br>LO9.1 use details and common knowledge to make sound inferences<br>LO9.2 draw accurate inferences from visuals<br>LO9.3 analyze tone in texts<br>LO9.4 choose an appropriate tone for writing assignment<br>LO9.5 analyze figurative language to make accurate inferences<br>LO9.6 use figurative language in writing.</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Everything in the tables above is copied <strong>verbatim</strong> from the university's FLM page (in English, as published) so you can check it against the copy your lecturer gives you: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13894\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13894</a> (needs your FPT login). If FLM publishes a newer syllabus, FLM wins.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Mọi thứ trong các bảng trên được chép <strong>nguyên văn</strong> từ trang FLM của trường (bằng tiếng Anh, đúng như trường công bố) để bạn đối chiếu với bản giảng viên phát: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13894\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13894</a> (cần đăng nhập tài khoản FPT). Nếu FLM công bố bản syllabus mới hơn thì theo FLM.</div></div>"
